  "worked_solution": "From the phase line, we can deduce the following:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-1$ and $y=3.$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along these lines.\n\n- $f(y)<0$ for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are negative in these regions.\n\n- $f(y)>0$ for $y\\in (-1,3).$ Therefore, the slopes of the slope field are positive in this region.\n\nThe only slope field that satisfies the above conditions is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14094575/assets/828432bf3e1afdb2d2e377d7d8af3272d765956120ce8aeaf5674fefa31365fd.png)",
